#
# Counter-example for math:NormPositiveDefiniteShape: a math:Norm induced by a
# math:SymmetricBilinearForm whose math:definiteness is math:indefinite. ‖x‖ = √⟨x, x⟩
# is a norm only for a positive-definite form. The form is named (so the
# math:inducedByForm minCount passes), so ONLY the sh:sparql positive-definiteness
# constraint fires. Validation MUST emit shacl.SPARQLConstraintComponent and no other
# finding (math:NonPositiveDefiniteNorm).
# Bound by tests/example-conformance.ttl (ex:ecNormIndefiniteForm).
@prefix math: <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/> .
@prefix ex:   <http://example.org/math/> .

ex:badNorm a math:Norm ;
    math:inducedByForm ex:indefForm .

ex:indefForm a math:SymmetricBilinearForm ;
    math:definiteness math:indefinite .
